# Direct calls to users-service (port 3001). Only the gateway is meant to call it,
# so every request needs the shared secret. Copy INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN from your .env.
# (REST Client variables are per file; don't commit the real value.)
@internal = PASTE-INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN-FROM-.env

### Create a user
POST http://localhost:3001/users
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "auth0Id": "auth0|test-123",
  "email": "joao@example.com",
  "name": "João"
}

### List users
GET http://localhost:3001/users
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}

### Get one user (paste an id from the list)
GET http://localhost:3001/users/PASTE-ID-HERE
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}

### Find by Auth0 id ("|" is written %7C)
GET http://localhost:3001/users/by-auth0/auth0%7Ctest-123
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}

### Change name / phone
PATCH http://localhost:3001/users/by-auth0/auth0%7Ctest-123
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "João Pedro", "phone": "+351912345678" }

### Invalid id → 400
GET http://localhost:3001/users/abc
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}

### Invalid email → 400
POST http://localhost:3001/users
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "auth0Id": "auth0|test-999", "email": "not-an-email" }

### Unknown field → 400
POST http://localhost:3001/users
X-Internal-Token: {{internal}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "auth0Id": "auth0|test-998", "email": "x@example.com", "role": "admin" }

### Duplicate → 409 (run the first "Create a user" request again)

### No secret → 401 (what anyone except the gateway gets)
GET http://localhost:3001/users
